{"type":"npc","name":"Postgeist","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":140,"temp":0,"max":140,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":30,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":null,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":60}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"all-damage","value":10,"exceptions":["fire","force","ghost-touch","spirit","vitality"],"doubleVs":["non-magical"]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"Truespeech, communicates through writing only"},"level":{"value":11},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>It is said that neither rain nor snow nor hail can keep the mail from being delivered. Sometimes, it turns out death itself can't stop the post.</p><p>Postgeists are formed when the employees of a postal service or other devoted messengers pass away in a time of great need. If the departed deliverers were sufficiently tenacious in their work, a part of their souls might fuse with psychic fragments of their raw determination, coalescing into a sentient being.</p><p>Postgeists see to the complete work of their departed forebears, using their telekinetic abilities to sort, file, and deliver letters with terrifying efficiency. The spirits never deviate from their appointed duties. Interlopers are booted aside with extreme prejudice, and a creature that dares flee from a delivery is chased to the ends of the world.</p><h2>Address Unknown</h2><p>Each postgeist has their own route, featuring favored postboxes, courier satchels, secret drop sites, and other mail repositories that they check unfailingly. Someone who knows a postgeist's route can use it to track down otherwise unfindable people. Simply address a letter to the quarry, wait for a postgeist to show up, and follow the postgeist—provided you can keep up with their unresting, all-weather travel pace.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 175/390/720 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Intimidation, Lore [Postal], Occultism, Society, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> constitution, death, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, sonic, void), force, intelligence, mirrored, sensory (darkvision), space, space shield, spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.5esP2GVzvxWsMgaX]{Environmental Endurance}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.6Ot4N22t5tPD51BO]{Knock}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.pwzdSlJgYqN7bs2w]{Telekinetic Hand}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.mrDi3v933gsmnw25]{Telekinetic Maneuver}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.69L70wKfGDY66Mk9]{Teleport}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.SwUiVavHKMWG7t5K]{Truespeech}), spirit, throwing, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Lachlan Carlsson-Forbes","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":-5},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":5},"wis":{"mod":7},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":22,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":20,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":24,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":20},"intimidation":{"base":21},"occultism":{"base":21},"society":{"base":22},"survival":{"base":24}},"traits":{"value":["incorporeal","spirit","undead"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"cVmnNTnajHN8Ihz5","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/postgeist.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Postgeist","displayName":0,"acto